# Shell scripts

- ShellCheck via `make lint-shell`
- Use `set -euo pipefail` in bash scripts
- SPDX header block with trailing blank line after the block
- Prefer existing `scripts/lib/*.sh` helpers over duplicating logic
- **CI gate quietness:** Scripts used as Makefile check leaves must source
  [`scripts/lib/check-quiet-env.sh`](../scripts/lib/check-quiet-env.sh), stay
  quiet on success by default, and stream tool output when
  `vlz_check_verbose_enabled` (`VLZ_CHECK_VERBOSE=1`). Capture tool stderr
  (including `eprintln!` / FR-022a path dumps and progress bars), not only
  `RUST_LOG`. Replay captured stderr on failure. Reference:
  [`scripts/benchmark-gate.sh`](../scripts/benchmark-gate.sh).
